INSERT INTO website_pages
  (id, page_group, title, slug, menu_label, summary, body, status, sort_order)
VALUES
(UUID(),'additional','Validate a PCMO Certificate','validate_certificate','Validate Certificate','Confirm the authenticity, current status, and credential record of a PCMO professional certificate quickly and reliably.','Certificate validation\n\nUse the credential identifier and recipient details shown on a PCMO certificate to request verification. Validation protects professional trust and helps employers, recruiters, and clients confirm that a credential is genuine and currently valid.\n\nWhat you can verify\n\nThe following details can be confirmed through the PCMO support team: credential title, recipient name, issue date, current status, the issuing PCMO programme, and the issuing organisation. Where a certificate has a unique credential identifier, quoting it speeds up the verification process.\n\nHow to request validation\n\nPrepare the credential identifier from the certificate, confirm the recipient name exactly as shown, and submit a validation request through the Contact page. Include the programme name and your relationship to the candidate (for example employer, recruitment agency, or client) so the team can respond efficiently.\n\nWhy validation matters\n\nCertification validation protects the integrity of professional credentials. It prevents misuse of PCMO branding, confirms that documented achievements are genuine, and gives employers confidence that a candidate has met the published programme requirements. PCMO takes the accuracy and security of its credential records seriously.\n\nPrivacy and records\n\nValidation confirms only the credential information published by PCMO. No other personal data is released through the validation process, and all requests are handled in line with PCMO privacy and data protection commitments.','published',200),
(UUID(),'additional','Associate Project Management Certified Professional','apmc','Associate Project Management Certified Professional (APMC)','Build a strong, recognised foundation for an early-career role in project management and demonstrate entry-level professional capability through an industry-recognised credential.','Programme overview\n\nThe Associate Project Management Certified Professional (APMC) pathway is PCMO''s entry-level certification for professionals beginning their project management journey. It introduces the complete project lifecycle, the language of projects, and the core disciplines that underpin successful delivery. The programme builds a structured foundation in project initiation, planning, execution, monitoring, and closure.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nOn completion, participants will be able to describe the project lifecycle and its key phases, support the development of project plans and schedules, help maintain scope, cost, quality, and risk information, communicate progress clearly to stakeholders, and contribute responsibly within a delivery team.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThe APMC is designed for early-career professionals, graduates, project assistants, coordinators, and professionals moving into project work from other disciplines. No prior formal project management qualification is required, making it an ideal starting point for building immediate confidence and credibility.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe programme covers project concepts and terminology, roles and responsibilities, project initiation and business cases, work breakdown structures and estimating, scheduling fundamentals, stakeholder identification and communication, quality basics, risk identification and logging, progress reporting, and professional conduct and ethics.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates complete a structured assessment consisting of multiple-choice knowledge checks and scenario-based questions. The assessment verifies understanding of core concepts, terminology, and practical judgement at an entry level. Preparation materials and practice questions are provided to support confident readiness.\n\nProfessional application\n\nAPMC holders can immediately apply their knowledge in supporting roles: maintaining project documentation, updating plans and registers, coordinating meetings and actions, preparing status updates, and contributing to risk and issue reviews. The credential signals dependable foundational knowledge to employers and creates a clear pathway toward intermediate and advanced project management certifications.\n\nDuration and format\n\nLearning is delivered through structured online modules that can be completed at your own pace, supported by practice activities, revision notes, and a final assessment. The recommended study time is clearly outlined in the programme handbook available on request.','published',210),
(UUID(),'additional','Project Management Essentials','project_management_essentials','Essentials of Project Management','Master the essential principles, tools, and controls used to initiate, plan, deliver, monitor, and close projects successfully across any industry.','Programme overview\n\nProject Management Essentials is a practical, accessible introduction to the language, tools, roles, and controls used across modern projects. It focuses on the essential building blocks every professional needs to contribute effectively to project delivery, whether working in a formal project management office or within an operational improvement initiative.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to define clear objectives and success criteria, create a work breakdown structure, sequence activities and build realistic schedules, identify and assign responsibilities, apply fundamental risk and change controls, and communicate progress in a structured way that supports confident decision-making.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis certification suits professionals who manage or support work packages, team leads, operational managers, engineers, analysts, and anyone who needs a dependable grounding in project working. It is also an excellent first certification for those planning a long-term career in project management.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers project definition and charters, stakeholders and governance, scope and requirements, work breakdown structures, estimating techniques, scheduling, roles and responsibilities, communication planning, risk and issue management, quality fundamentals, change control, progress reporting, and lessons learned.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nAssessment combines knowledge checks with scenario-based questions that test practical application. Candidates must demonstrate that they can connect concepts to realistic workplace situations and select appropriate tools and responses for common delivery challenges.\n\nProfessional application\n\nEssentials-trained professionals add immediate value by bringing structure to day-to-day delivery: translating objectives into deliverables, tracking progress against plans, escalating concerns early, applying change control discipline, and capturing lessons that improve future delivery. The certification strengthens both competence and confidence in any team environment.\n\nDuration and format\n\nThe programme is delivered online through self-paced modules with practical exercises, revision materials, and a final assessment. Expected study effort and support options are documented in the certification handbook available on request.','published',220),
(UUID(),'additional','Introduction to Project Management','introduction_project_management','Introduction to Project Management','Start your project management journey with core concepts, essential terminology, the project lifecycle, and the roles that make delivery successful.','Programme overview\n\nIntroduction to Project Management explores why projects are created, how success is defined, and how ideas become controlled results. It explains the core concepts, terminology, and roles that underpin every project, giving newcomers a reliable mental model for navigating any delivery environment.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will understand the project lifecycle from initiation through closure, be able to describe key terms such as scope, deliverable, milestone, stakeholder, and governance, recognise the responsibilities of sponsors, managers, and team members, and apply fundamental planning and monitoring concepts to simple scenarios.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is ideal for students, recent graduates, aspiring project coordinators, administrative professionals, and technical specialists who work alongside project teams and want to speak the language of projects confidently.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus introduces projects versus operations, the project lifecycle, defining success, initiation and the business case, planning, execution and monitoring, closure and handover, stakeholders and communication, governance structures, and continuous improvement through lessons learned.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates complete a knowledge-based assessment covering terminology, lifecycle phases, roles, and basic judgement scenarios. The assessment confirms readiness to contribute to project support activity and provides a springboard to more advanced PCMO programmes.\n\nProfessional application\n\nGraduates can apply structured thinking immediately: assisting with project documentation, supporting planning workshops, preparing status summaries, maintaining action and risk registers, and communicating effectively with stakeholders. The credential builds early professional credibility and career momentum.\n\nDuration and format\n\nOnline, self-paced modules with interactive activities and a final assessment. Detailed programme information, including recommended study hours, is available in the certification handbook on request.','published',230),
(UUID(),'additional','Project Management Fundamentals','project_management_fundamentals','Project Management Fundamentals','Develop dependable, practical skills across scope, schedule, cost, quality, risk, and stakeholder management for real-world project delivery.','Programme overview\n\nProject Management Fundamentals builds a practical, dependable foundation for coordinating work and supporting successful delivery. It goes beyond terminology to develop the day-to-day skills professionals use to manage scope, time, cost, quality, resources, and risk on real projects.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to translate objectives into clear deliverables, break work into manageable packages, sequence and estimate activities, build and maintain realistic schedules, monitor performance against baselines, manage change, and communicate decisions with confidence and clarity.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThe programme is designed for project coordinators, assistant project managers, team leads, engineers, operations staff, and professionals who need a strong operational grounding in project management practice before progressing to advanced or leadership programmes.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers scope definition and control, requirements gathering, work breakdown structures, estimating and budgeting, critical-path scheduling, resource allocation, responsibility assignment, risk management, quality assurance, communication and reporting, change control, and performance measurement.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nAssessment includes knowledge checks, practical planning exercises, and scenario-based questions that test judgement. Candidates demonstrate the ability to apply tools and techniques to realistic project situations and explain the reasoning behind their decisions.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders immediately improve their contribution to project teams: building clearer plans, tracking progress honestly, identifying and escalating risk, managing requests for change, and producing reports that support informed decisions. This certification strengthens employability for coordination and management roles across industries.\n\nDuration and format\n\nDelivered as structured online modules with practical exercises, templates, and a final assessment. Study guidance and support details are contained in the certification handbook available on request.','published',240),
(UUID(),'additional','Agile Project Management','agile_project_management','Agile Project Management','Learn how adaptive planning, iterative delivery, and continuous feedback enable teams to create value sooner and respond confidently to change.','Programme overview\n\nAgile Project Management explores how agile values, principles, and practices support delivery in uncertain and fast-moving environments. The programme explains how iterative planning, incremental delivery, and structured reflection allow teams to respond to change while keeping stakeholders informed and outcomes on track.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will understand agile values and principles, be able to work with product backlogs, plan iterations, run effective reviews and retrospectives, manage stakeholder expectations, and adapt delivery plans responsibly without sacrificing transparency or quality.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis certification suits project managers, developers, product owners, business analysts, delivery leads, and team members working in agile environments who want to strengthen their coaching, planning, and facilitation capability.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers agile values and principles, scrum and kanban, roles and responsibilities, product backlogs and prioritisation, iteration planning, user stories, estimation in agile, daily working practices, reviews and demonstrations, retrospectives, velocity and flow, and scaling considerations.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates are assessed through scenario-based questions, planning exercises, and knowledge checks that test understanding of agile practices and the judgement required to apply them in real delivery contexts.\n\nProfessional application\n\nGraduates can facilitate better planning conversations, protect delivery focus, make priorities visible, remove obstacles systematically, and use feedback to improve both the product and the way the team works. The credential demonstrates modern, collaborative delivery capability valued across technology, product, and transformation environments.\n\nDuration and format\n\nSelf-paced online modules, practical exercises, and a final assessment. Programme details and recommended study effort are available in the certification handbook on request.','published',250),
(UUID(),'additional','Advanced Project Management','advanced_project_management','Advanced Project Management','Lead complex delivery environments with stronger governance, integrated controls, commercial awareness, and confident leadership.','Programme overview\n\nAdvanced Project Management prepares experienced professionals to lead complex delivery environments. It builds on foundational capability to address strategic alignment, complexity, assurance, benefits management, commercial awareness, and the leadership behaviours required to guide multidisciplinary teams through uncertainty.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to balance competing constraints across scope, time, cost, and risk, interpret performance and assurance evidence, govern change confidently, recover challenged projects, and lead multidisciplinary teams with clarity, accountability, and professional judgement.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is aimed at project managers, senior coordinators, programme staff, team leads, and specialists preparing for greater responsibility over complex, high-value, or multi-stakeholder delivery.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers strategic alignment and business cases, complexity and uncertainty, integrated planning and control, earned value and performance analysis, assurance and audit, benefits management, commercial awareness and contracts, change and transformation, stakeholder strategy, and leading through challenge and recovery.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nAssessment combines knowledge checks, scenario-based exercises, and practical case analysis requiring candidates to evaluate evidence, weigh options, and justify decisions at an advanced level. Responses are marked against explicit criteria explained in the programme handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nAdvanced certification signals readiness for senior delivery roles. Holders bring stronger governance discipline, sharper performance insight, and the confidence to recover challenged work, engage sponsors constructively, and align delivery activity with what the organisation actually values.\n\nDuration and format\n\nAdvanced online modules, case studies, reflection activities, and a comprehensive final assessment. Participation guidance and assessment rules are documented in the certification handbook available on request.','published',260),
(UUID(),'additional','Strategic Project Management','strategic_project_management','Strategic Project Management','Connect project decisions with organisational strategy, value, portfolio priorities, and the long-term outcomes that matter most to leaders.','Programme overview\n\nStrategic Project Management shifts the focus from delivering outputs to creating organisational value. It explores portfolio alignment, business cases, benefits realisation, investment decisions, governance at scale, and the strategic risk conversations that guide whether projects should be started, continued, adjusted, or stopped.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to evaluate whether projects remain aligned with strategy and value, engage sponsors around outcomes rather than outputs, shape business cases and investment options, and communicate evidence-based recommendations that support confident executive decisions.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThe programme is designed for senior project managers, portfolio and PMO professionals, programme managers, sponsors, and functional leaders who influence capital, transformation, and delivery investment decisions.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers strategy formulation and delivery, portfolio selection and prioritisation, business case development and assurance, benefits mapping and realisation, governance and investment decision forums, strategic risk and uncertainty, organisational change, performance and value reporting, and the role of the project leader in executive conversations.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates complete scenario-based assessments and a structured business-case exercise that tests their ability to evaluate options, quantify value, and present reasoned recommendations. Detailed assessment guidance is provided in the programme handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders bring a strategic lens to delivery: they ask better questions about value, design benefit-focused outcomes, challenge scope and spend intelligently, and build governance environments where decisions are made on evidence. This certification prepares professionals for portfolio, PMO, and senior leadership pathways.\n\nDuration and format\n\nSelf-paced strategic modules, case discussions, exercises, and a final assessment. Full programme details are available in the certification handbook on request.','published',270),
(UUID(),'additional','Certified Project Manager Preparation','cpm_preparation','Certified Project Manager (CPM) Preparation','Prepare systematically for professional project management assessment with structured study goals, practice questions, and exam readiness techniques.','Programme overview\n\nThe Certified Project Manager (CPM) Preparation pathway is a focused readiness programme for professionals preparing to attempt a professional project management certification assessment. It reviews the full project lifecycle, knowledge domains, scenario analysis, professional judgement, and the assessment techniques needed to perform with confidence.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to structure a realistic study plan, apply core knowledge across all major project management domains, approach scenario questions methodically, review performance evidence, and manage time and pressure effectively during assessment.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is intended for experienced practitioners and project managers who have consolidated practical experience and are now seeking formal professional certification through a structured, disciplined preparation route.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus offers a structured review of the project lifecycle, integration and governance, scope, schedule, cost, quality, resource, communication, risk, procurement, and stakeholder management, alongside ethical practice, scenario-based question techniques, performance analysis, and revision and examination strategy.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nPreparation centres on a full mock assessment and practice banks that mirror the professional exam format. Candidates receive guidance on evidence review, question interpretation, answer structuring, and the rules that govern exam conduct, reassessment, and appeals.\n\nProfessional application\n\nSuccessful candidates enter the certification assessment with a clear study strategy and reduced uncertainty. The preparation discipline also strengthens daily practice: sharper prioritisation, better self-review, and more confident professional judgement on real projects.\n\nDuration and format\n\nThe pathway combines structured revision modules, practice question banks, mock assessments, and a personal readiness tracker. Compulsory preparation rules are documented in the programme handbook available on request.','published',280),
(UUID(),'additional','Program Management','program_management','Program Management','Coordinate related projects and activities to achieve strategic benefits that individual projects cannot deliver on their own.','Programme overview\n\nProgram Management develops the discipline of coordinating related projects, workstreams, and business change to deliver benefits beyond the reach of any single project. It covers program vision, governance, dependency and risk management, benefits realisation, stakeholder alignment, and the managed transition of outcomes into operations.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to build an integrated roadmap across projects, manage cross-project dependencies and risk, track benefit realisation credibly, resolve competing priorities, and sustain strategic alignment through transparent governance.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThe programme suits senior project managers, program managers, PMO leaders, portfolio professionals, transformation leads, and executives accountable for delivering multi-project change.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers program definition and business case, governance structures, blueprint and design, dependency mapping, resource management across projects, cross-programme risk, benefits management and measurement, stakeholder and communication strategy, quality and assurance, financial management, and transition to business-as-usual.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nAssessment includes scenario-based questions and a program-level practical exercise covering dependency analysis, benefits tracking, and governance decision-making. Assessment guidance and success criteria are detailed in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders can lead multi-project initiatives with better alignment, foresight, and control: coordinating delivery, surfacing conflicts early, protecting benefits focus, and creating honest reporting that enables sponsors and boards to steer effectively. This certification is a recognised credential for program and transformation leadership roles.\n\nDuration and format\n\nAdvanced online modules, program scenario exercises, and a final assessment. Programme duration, support, and rules are documented in the certification handbook available on request.','published',290),
(UUID(),'additional','PMO Implementation','pmo_implementation','PMO (Project Management Office) Implementation','Design and implement a Project Management Office that improves governance, insight, capability, and measurable delivery value.','Programme overview\n\nPMO Implementation provides a practical, structured approach to designing and standing up a Project Management Office. It guides participants through assessing organisational needs, selecting an appropriate PMO model, defining services, establishing governance, choosing meaningful measures, and planning adoption so the PMO improves delivery rather than adding bureaucracy.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to diagnose current delivery challenges, recommend an appropriate PMO model and service portfolio, design governance and reporting that supports decisions, select measures that matter, and build an adoption plan that earns stakeholder support.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is for professionals establishing, maturing, or rescoping a PMO: PMO leads and analysts, project leaders, transformation managers, and executives sponsoring a new or revitalised delivery support function.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers PMO models and value propositions, maturity assessment, service design, governance frameworks, portfolio and project reporting, resource and capacity management, tooling and process, benefits and performance measures, change management and adoption, and demonstrating and communicating value.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates complete scenario-based questions and a PMO design exercise in which they develop a tailored implementation plan. Assessment expectations are explained in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders design PMOs that enable decisions, build capability, simplify controls, and demonstrate measurable value. The certification equips professionals to lead PMO set-up conversations, secure stakeholder buy-in, and avoid the common failure modes of process-heavy, value-light support functions.\n\nDuration and format\n\nStructured online modules, practical templates, a design exercise, and a final assessment. Full programme information is available in the certification handbook on request.','published',300),
(UUID(),'additional','Project Management Leadership','project_management_leadership','Project Management Leadership','Lead project teams with clarity, trust, accountability, and professional judgement in complex and changing environments.','Programme overview\n\nProject Management Leadership explores what it takes to lead project teams effectively: developing direction, building trust, creating accountability, and exercising sound professional judgement. It combines leadership theory with practical techniques for motivating teams, managing conflict, influencing stakeholders, and making decisions under pressure.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to create and communicate a clear project vision, build psychological safety and productive team norms, address performance and conflict constructively, influence without formal authority, and guide stakeholders through ambiguity and change with integrity.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is designed for project managers, team leads, subject-matter experts leading others, and professionals preparing for leadership responsibility over people, delivery, and stakeholder relationships.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers leadership styles and identity, team development, motivation and engagement, delegation and empowerment, coaching and feedback, conflict and difficult conversations, decision-making and judgement, influence and negotiation, change leadership, ethical leadership, and resilience.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nAssessment combines scenario-based questions with a leadership reflection exercise requiring candidates to analyse a real or realistic situation and propose a sound leadership approach. Guidance on assessment expectations is provided in the handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders create more cohesive, accountable, and resilient teams. They communicate purpose, build trust, resolve tension early, and guide people through uncertainty, which directly improves delivery performance and reduces the friction that erodes results. The certification supports progression into senior project and programme leadership roles.\n\nDuration and format\n\nSelf-paced modules, reflective exercises, and a final assessment. Detailed programme and assessment information is available in the certification handbook on request.','published',310),
(UUID(),'additional','Introduction to Contract Management','introduction_contract_management','Introduction to Contract Management','Understand the contract lifecycle, key obligations, and the practical responsibilities that protect value, relationships, and delivery on both sides.','Programme overview\n\nIntroduction to Contract Management follows a contract from planning and formation through mobilisation, administration, performance, change, closeout, and lessons learned. It explains the responsibilities of each party, the importance of disciplined records and communication, and how good contract management protects value and working relationships.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will understand the stages of the contract lifecycle, maintain obligations, notices, deliverables, and decisions, handle routine commercial correspondence professionally, support performance and change management, and contribute to a disciplined, auditable contract record.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThe programme is ideal for early-career commercial professionals, project coordinators, engineers, buyers, administrators, and anyone who works with contracts and needs a reliable understanding of how they operate day to day.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers contract formation and structure, contract law basics, terms and conditions, roles and responsibilities, mobilisation, administration and records, performance management, variations and change, payments and invoicing, claims awareness, closeout and handover, and lessons learned.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates complete knowledge checks and scenario-based questions covering the contract lifecycle, key obligations, and routine commercial judgement. Assessment rules and preparation guidance are provided in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nGraduates handle contract activity with greater confidence and discipline: tracking obligations, managing correspondence, following notice requirements, supporting variation control, and keeping the accurate records that prevent disputes. This credential is a strong foundation for a career in contract and commercial management.\n\nDuration and format\n\nOnline, self-paced modules with practical examples and a final assessment. Recommended study hours and support options are documented in the certification handbook available on request.','published',320),
(UUID(),'additional','Contract Administration Fundamentals','contract_administration_fundamentals','Contract Administration Fundamentals','Apply reliable day-to-day controls for obligations, records, correspondence, changes, payments, and performance under contract.','Programme overview\n\nContract Administration Fundamentals builds the practical disciplines needed to administer a contract fairly, consistently, and accurately. It focuses on the systems, behaviours, and records that keep a contract healthy: tracking deliverables, managing correspondence, reviewing applications, documenting decisions, controlling changes, and maintaining an auditable trail.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to administer routine contract activities to a professional standard, maintain accurate contract registers and files, process applications and payments correctly, identify and document variations, support performance conversations, and protect the organisation through disciplined record-keeping.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThe programme is designed for contract administrators, commercial assistants, project coordinators, procurement staff, and technical personnel who administer contracts as part of a wider role and need dependable practical control.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers contract documentation and registers, obligations and deliverables, correspondence and notices, performance monitoring, payment and invoicing cycles, variations and change control, extensions of time, delay awareness, records and evidence, meetings and minutes, closeout, and risk of poor administration.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nAssessment uses scenario-based questions and practical administration exercises that test the application of controls to realistic contract situations. Success criteria and preparation materials are provided in the handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders bring order and reliability to contract operations: fewer missed obligations, cleaner records, faster responses, and earlier visibility of problems. Strong administration is the first line of defence against disputes, and this certification builds exactly that capability.\n\nDuration and format\n\nSelf-paced online modules, worked examples, templates, and a final assessment. Details are available in the certification handbook on request.','published',330),
(UUID(),'additional','Negotiation Skills for Contract Management','contract_negotiation_skills','Negotiation Skills for Contract Management','Prepare and conduct principled negotiations that protect commercial value while building durable, ethical working relationships.','Programme overview\n\nContract Negotiation Skills equips professionals with a structured approach to negotiation: preparing thoroughly, understanding interests versus positions, generating options, handling authority and concessions, and documenting agreements clearly. The programme emphasises principled negotiation that creates value while protecting relationships.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to prepare a negotiation plan with clear objectives, gather and evaluate evidence, listen actively and probe effectively, present structured proposals, manage tactics and pressure, obtain the right approvals, and document outcomes accurately.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is for contract managers, buyers, commercial leads, project managers, and professionals who regularly negotiate scope, price, risk, or terms with suppliers, clients, or partners.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers negotiation fundamentals, preparation and strategy, interests and positions, BATNA and walk-away, options for mutual gain, communication and questioning, concessions and trade-offs, managing difficult behaviours, cultural considerations, authority and delegation, closing and documenting, and ethics.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates complete scenario-based questions and a negotiation simulation exercise demonstrated through structured analysis. Assessment criteria are detailed in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders negotiate with greater confidence and preparation: clearer objectives, stronger use of evidence, better listening, and outcomes that are both commercially sound and relationship-positive. The certification strengthens professional credibility in commercial and delivery roles alike.\n\nDuration and format\n\nStructured online modules, practical negotiation scenarios, and a final assessment. Full programme information is available in the certification handbook on request.','published',340),
(UUID(),'additional','Advanced Contract Management Strategies','advanced_contract_management','Advanced Contract Management Strategies','Manage complex commercial relationships, risk, change, performance, and disputes strategically across high-value contracts.','Programme overview\n\nAdvanced Contract Management Strategies equips experienced professionals to manage complex, high-value contracts strategically. It explores advanced governance, commercial strategy, performance and incentive regimes, claims avoidance, dispute management, and the relationship health that sustains long-term value.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to design and operate governance that matches contract complexity, integrate legal, commercial, operational, and stakeholder evidence in decisions, manage performance and incentive mechanisms, prevent claims before they crystallise, and steer disputes toward constructive resolution.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is aimed at senior contract managers, commercial managers, procurement leaders, project directors, and legal professionals who manage significant contract exposure and need a strategic commercial toolkit.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers contract strategy and structuring, complex governance, commercial and pricing models, performance and KPIs, incentive and remedy regimes, risk and opportunity management, change and claims avoidance, delay and disruption, dispute resolution options, relationship management, and exit and transition planning.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nAssessment combines advanced scenario analysis, a commercial judgement exercise, and evidence-based written responses. Detailed criteria and marking guidance are provided in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders guide high-value contracts with confidence: aligning commercial frameworks with delivery reality, protecting margin and value, preventing disputes through good practice, and leading negotiations with sophisticated stakeholders. The credential supports senior commercial leadership pathways.\n\nDuration and format\n\nAdvanced online modules, case studies, and a comprehensive final assessment. Programme rules and support details are documented in the certification handbook available on request.','published',350),
(UUID(),'additional','Legal Aspects of Contract Management','legal_aspects_contract_management','Legal Aspects of Contract Management','Understand the legal principles that shape contract formation, interpretation, performance, and remedies, and apply them responsibly.','Programme overview\n\nLegal Aspects of Contract Management provides a practical, non-technical understanding of the legal principles governing contracts. It covers authority, offer, acceptance, consideration, terms, interpretation, breach, damages, termination, and dispute resolution, so commercial professionals can recognise issues early and act within their authority.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will understand the foundations of contract formation and interpretation, be able to identify legal risk in common commercial situations, maintain evidence that protects positions, follow delegated authority, and know when to escalate for qualified legal advice.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThe programme is for contract managers, commercial staff, buyers, project managers, engineers, and finance professionals who work with contracts and need legal awareness to complement their commercial skills.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers sources of law, formation of contracts, written and oral terms, interpretation rules, conditions and warranties, exclusion and limitation clauses, privity and third parties, breach and remedies, damages, termination and repudiation, misrepresentation and duress, and methods of dispute resolution.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates complete scenario-based questions focusing on recognising legal issues and taking appropriate, responsible action. Assessment expectations and preparation notes are provided in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders make more legally mature decisions: drafting and reviewing terms with sharper awareness, managing notices and deadlines correctly, preserving evidence, and escalating issues before they become disputes. This certification reduces personal and organisational exposure and complements advanced commercial training.\n\nDuration and format\n\nSelf-paced modules, illustrative case examples, and a final assessment. Programme details are documented in the certification handbook available on request.','published',360),
(UUID(),'additional','Relationship Management in Contracts','relationship_management_contracts','Relationship Management in Contracts','Build collaborative commercial relationships without weakening accountability, controls, or contract integrity.','Programme overview\n\nRelationship Management in Contracts explores how to build trust, alignment, and joint improvement in commercial relationships while retaining the controls that protect both parties. It covers governance forums, communication protocols, performance conversations, escalation, and the behaviours that turn contracts from transactional documents into productive partnerships.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to establish effective relationship governance, run productive performance and review meetings, manage conflict and escalation professionally, separate people from problems, and maintain a disciplined focus on shared outcomes.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is designed for contract managers, account managers, supplier relationship leads, project managers, and anyone responsible for day-to-day working relationships with clients, suppliers, or partners.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers relationship maturity, trust and credibility, governance and steering groups, communication protocols, performance and service reviews, joint improvement initiatives, managing disagreements, escalation and exit, cultural awareness, and balancing relationship with contract discipline.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nAssessment uses scenario-based questions and a relationship-management exercise testing practical judgement in realistic commercial situations. Assessment details are provided in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders build relationships that prevent problems rather than simply reacting to them: earlier conversations, shared evidence, and joint problem-solving. The result is fewer disputes, smoother change, and better whole-life value for both parties.\n\nDuration and format\n\nOnline modules, practical relationship scenarios, and a final assessment. Recommended study hours are documented in the certification handbook available on request.','published',370),
(UUID(),'additional','Strategic Contract Management','strategic_contract_management','Strategic Contract Management','Align contract strategy, supplier performance, risk, and value with the organisation broad commercial priorities.','Programme overview\n\nStrategic Contract Management connects contract activity to organisational priorities. It explores category objectives, sourcing decisions, contract design, governance, performance, innovation, and exit planning, giving senior professionals the frameworks to manage contracts as strategic assets rather than administrative overhead.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to align contract strategies with business strategy, prioritise management attention across a portfolio, design contracts that allocate risk and unlock value, build performance and innovation into relationships, and plan resilient exits and transitions.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is for senior contract managers, category and procurement leaders, commercial directors, and executives accountable for supplier value, risk, and continuity.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers strategy and value, category management, sourcing and supplier selection, contract design and risk allocation, commercial models, governance and assurance, performance and innovation management, supply chain resilience, and exit and transition planning.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates complete scenario analysis and a strategic exercise developing or critiquing a contract strategy. Assessment expectations and criteria are documented in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders shift from managing contracts reactively to shaping them deliberately: allocating attention where risk and value are highest, designing for outcomes, protecting continuity, and improving whole-life value. The certification prepares professionals for commercial leadership and executive advisory roles.\n\nDuration and format\n\nAdvanced self-paced modules, strategy exercises, and a final assessment. Full programme information is available in the certification handbook on request.','published',380),
(UUID(),'additional','Ethics and Compliance in Contract Management','contract_ethics_compliance','Ethics and Compliance in Contract Management','Make transparent, fair, accountable, and compliant decisions throughout the entire contract lifecycle.','Programme overview\n\nEthics and Compliance in Contract Management examines the standards that protect trust in commercial practice: conflicts of interest, confidentiality, anti-bribery and corruption controls, competition, records, approvals, gifts and hospitality, and the duty to report concerns. It builds the professional judgement and moral courage needed to uphold integrity under pressure.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will be able to identify ethical and compliance risks in contract activity, apply policy and law consistently, document judgement and decisions, challenge improper conduct appropriately, and protect the reputation of their organisation and the profession.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThis programme is relevant to every professional who handles contracts, procurement, finance, or commercial relationships, and is essential for those in governance, audit, or compliance roles with oversight of commercial practice.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers ethical frameworks, conflicts of interest, confidentiality and data, bribery and corruption, gifts and hospitality, competition and fairness, responsible sourcing, record integrity, approvals and authority, whistle-blowing and reporting, and the consequences of misconduct.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nAssessment uses scenario-based questions and an ethics case exercise requiring candidates to apply principles and policy to demanding situations. Guidance is provided in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders create a more trustworthy commercial environment: stronger controls, informed judgement, and the confidence to raise concerns constructively. This certification strengthens personal accountability and is valuable evidence of professional integrity for employers and partners.\n\nDuration and format\n\nSelf-paced modules, case-based discussions, and a final assessment. Programme details are documented in the certification handbook available on request.','published',390),
(UUID(),'additional','International Contract Management','international_contract_management','International Contract Management','Navigate cross-border contracts with confidence across legal systems, cultures, currencies, logistics, and international dispute forums.','Programme overview\n\nInternational Contract Management prepares professionals to operate effectively across borders. It explores governing law and jurisdiction, international trade terms, arbitration, tax, currency, sanctions, language, and cultural expectations, so contracts can be structured and managed to reduce cross-border risk and protect value.\n\nLearning outcomes\n\nParticipants will understand how to choose and manage governing law and dispute forums, apply international trade terms and incoterms correctly, plan for currency and tax exposure, respect sanctions and export controls, and communicate effectively across cultures and languages.\n\nWho should attend\n\nThe programme suits contract and commercial managers, procurement professionals, project leaders, legal advisors, and exporters involved in cross-border, multi-jurisdictional, or international delivery.\n\nKey topics covered\n\nThe syllabus covers international legal systems, governing law and jurisdiction, arbitration and mediation, trade terms and incoterms, cross-border documents, currency and payment, taxation, customs and logistics, sanctions and compliance, language and translation, and cultural dimensions of negotiation and management.\n\nAssessment approach\n\nCandidates complete scenario-based questions and a cross-border contract exercise covering risk allocation, forum selection, and practical coordination. Assessment details are provided in the certification handbook.\n\nProfessional application\n\nHolders plan for cross-border complexity early: allocating risk clearly, coordinating specialist advice, structuring payment and delivery terms, and building resilient relationships with international counterparts. The certification enhances capability for global and export-driven roles.\n\nDuration and format\n\nStructured online modules, international case studies, and a final assessment. Programme information is documented in the certification handbook available on request.','published',400),
(UUID(),'additional','Join the Conversation','join_the_conversation','Join the Conversation','Participate in professional discussions and share practical insight with the PCMO community.','Community participation\n\nDiscover featured discussions, contribute relevant experience, ask thoughtful questions, and learn from diverse professional perspectives. The PCMO community brings together practitioners across projects, contracts, procurement, and transformation.\n\nCommunity standards\n\nKeep contributions respectful, evidence-informed, constructive, inclusive, and focused on professional learning. Every member helps create a space where ideas can be tested kindly and practical insight can be shared openly.\n\nGetting started\n\nCreate a profile, review the community guidelines, and join conversations that match your experience and interests. Thoughtful questions and well-grounded answers are always welcome.','published',410)
